    <header>
      <span class="eyebrow">Institutional Standards</span>
      <h1>Evidence Synthesis Protocol & Review Methodology</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">The editorial framework for reviewing evidence across the Star Research Library to evaluate neurobiology, nootropic substances, and cognitive claims without commercial influence.</p>
    </header>

    <section>
      <h2>1. Purpose and Scope</h2>
      <p>The Star Research Library provides independent, critical assessments of chemical compounds, botanicals, and physiological interventions. Each monograph synthesizes available evidence to determine what scientific literature establishes, what remains contested, and what current evidence cannot verify.</p>
      <div class="rule-callout">
        <strong>The Foundational Epistemic Rule:</strong> Mechanistic plausibility must never be presented as demonstrated clinical efficacy. Biochemical activity in an assay or animal model does not establish human cognitive enhancement.
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>2. Evidence Grading Matrix</h2>
      <p>Study-design labels describe the type of evidence. Confidence is assessed separately using risk of bias, precision, consistency, and applicability. A label alone does not establish high certainty.</p>

<div class="tier-stack"><div class="tier-card"><strong class="tier-badge">H1</strong><div><h4>Systematic review or meta-analysis of controlled human studies</h4></div></div><div class="tier-card"><strong class="tier-badge">H2</strong><div><h4>Randomized controlled human trial</h4></div></div><div class="tier-card"><strong class="tier-badge">H3</strong><div><h4>Controlled or nonrandomized human study</h4></div></div><div class="tier-card"><strong class="tier-badge">H4</strong><div><h4>Observational human evidence</h4></div></div><div class="tier-card"><strong class="tier-badge">P1</strong><div><h4>Animal / in-vivo evidence</h4></div></div><div class="tier-card"><strong class="tier-badge">P2</strong><div><h4>In-vitro / cellular evidence</h4></div></div><div class="tier-card"><strong class="tier-badge">M</strong><div><h4>Mechanistic or theoretical evidence</h4></div></div><div class="tier-card"><strong class="tier-badge">A</strong><div><h4>Anecdotal or historical report</h4></div></div></div><p>Confidence: High, Moderate, Low, Very Low, or Not rated. Anecdotes and historical reports provide context, not proof of efficacy.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>3. Literature Screening & Synthesis Standards</h2>
      <p>The following is the target review process. Existing bibliography entries and author-submitted narrative reviews may have incomplete verification; their publication does not certify completion of this process:</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Database Search:</strong> Record the databases actually searched, dates, search terms, eligibility criteria, and screening decisions. Relevant sources may include PubMed/MEDLINE, Embase where accessible, Cochrane Library, and trial registries.</li>
        <li><strong>Methodological Filtration:</strong> Non-peer-reviewed white papers, industry marketing dossiers, and forum anecdotes are excluded from evidentiary grading.</li>
        <li><strong>Dosage and Translation Verification:</strong> Identify species, route, exposure, and limitations of translating animal results. Dose scaling alone does not establish a safe or effective human dose; monographs do not provide self-dosing guidance.</li>
        <li><strong>Conflict of Interest Audit:</strong> Document available funding and author disclosures, and flag missing information. A disclosed relationship does not by itself determine a study’s validity.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>4. Institutional Separation</h2>
      <p>Monographs document pharmacological data regardless of whether a compound is lawful as a dietary supplement or prohibited from commerce. The presence of a compound in our library reflects academic relevance, not retail availability. For comprehensive governance policies, consult our formal institutional standards.</p>
    </section>

    <footer>
      <p>Star Nootropics · Evidence Review Protocol v1.0 · Governed under the <a href="/policy">Research Independence & Editorial Policy</a>.</p>
    </footer>
  </Layout>